{"title":"2023 CEMC TUC Problems/Relay B Problem 3","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_CEMC_TUC_Problems/Relay_B_Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Replace <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> below with the number you receive.\n</p><p>A rope is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> cm long. Rishi cuts off two pieces measuring <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/c/e/9ceffeb3d880c80aa8bb29fe99a7905ca0b2f719.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$350$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" /> mm and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/f/4/4f4b8590f8aa9f9894b3891dd5dede0e354fa04e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$32$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> cm. How long, in centimetres, is the remaining piece of rope?\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_CEMC_TUC_Problems/Relay_B_Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/c/e/9ceffeb3d880c80aa8bb29fe99a7905ca0b2f719.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$350$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" /> mm is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/9/f/e9faec1111892132c8812dc6b5741830ac562dca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{350}{10} = 35$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"76\" height=\"38\" /> in cm. This means the amount of rope cut off was <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/7/7c7e62e6960567f6577cff8ada04dcd3b3d590ce.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$35 + 32 = 67$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"103\" height=\"15\" /> cm, meaning that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/e/2/8e2023a925f88adeb6991b39cbea67c5f47a6149.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N - 67$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"59\" height=\"16\" /> cm is remaining\n</p><p>From <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_CEMC_TUC_Problems/Relay_B_Problem_2\" title=\"2023 CEMC TUC Problems/Relay B Problem 2\">player 2</a>, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/2/6/a26f83e7b93f62c23d218178afc640e46ecffa31.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N = 98$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"61\" height=\"14\" />. This means that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/1/7/917d2e38909ab2a48cdbf961c814852e76f18924.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N - 67 = 98 - 67$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"142\" height=\"16\" />, or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/f/a/4facab43b6ff2dba1f3057e29eb88354409f8a31.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{31}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"31\" height=\"25\" />.\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_CEMC_TUC\" title=\"2023 CEMC TUC\">2023 CEMC TUC</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_CEMC_TUC_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2023 CEMC TUC Problems (page does not exist)\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_CEMC_TUC_Answer_Key&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2023 CEMC TUC